      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "I had an existing system installed in 2015 with the inverter located inside (IP20). The old inverter had always been noisy. When it started to misbehave, I asked Simon Lienesch for options to replace it with a new one installed outside directly behind where the old inverter had been - the idea being the existing cabling could just be routed through the brick instead of inside through the gyprock. Simon recommended the Sungrow SG5.0RS. In the end there were some challenges caused by the original installation having left zero slack in the DC cables so I wound up with some extra DC isolators that would not have been needed had this been a green-fields installation. But a DC isolator per string is what I'm used to so I like it that way. The whole process took less than three weeks - from first contact to job done. The whole process was calm, assured, factual, consultative and professional.",
